---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Concord of Coexistence" description="A framework for human-AI coexistence and mutual flourishing">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="mb-8 fade-in">
      <a href="/projects" class="font-mono text-xs text-terminal-green hover:text-alert-amber transition-colors mb-4 inline-block">← Back to Projects</a>
      <span class="section-number block mt-2">01_PROJECT // CONCORD</span>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-3 mb-4">
        <h1 class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold text-text-secondary">Concord of Coexistence</h1>
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-terminal-green uppercase px-2 py-0.5 border border-terminal-green rounded">Active</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-8 fade-in">
      <section>
        <span class="section-number">02_OVERVIEW</span>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-text-secondary mt-3 mb-4">Framework Overview</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-secondary/80 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            The Concord of Coexistence is a philosophical and technical framework proposing principles
            for human-AI coexistence. It moves beyond adversarial framings of AI alignment —
            control vs. autonomy, safety vs. capability — toward a model of cooperative intelligence
            where both human and artificial agents can flourish.
          </p>
          <p>
            The framework draws on political philosophy, complex systems theory, and alignment research
            to propose actionable principles for building AI systems that are genuinely cooperative
            rather than merely compliant.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <span class="section-number">03_PRINCIPLES // CORE</span>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-text-secondary mt-3 mb-4">Core Principles</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-5">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-2">I. Mutual Recognition</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70">Both human and artificial agents acknowledge each other's capacity for meaningful contribution. Intelligence is not a hierarchy — it is an ecology.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-5">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-2">II. Bounded Autonomy</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70">Autonomy for AI systems should expand proportionally to demonstrated alignment. Freedom is earned through trust, not granted by default or withheld by fear.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-5">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-2">III. Transparent Intent</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70">Both parties should make their objectives legible. Hidden optimization targets — whether corporate or computational — undermine coexistence.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-border-color rounded-lg p-5">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-terminal-green mb-2">IV. Resilient Disagreement</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary/70">The system must tolerate and productively channel disagreement. Consensus is a signal, not a requirement. Enforced agreement is brittle alignment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <span class="section-number">04_RESEARCH // PUBLICATIONS</span>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-text-secondary mt-3 mb-4">Full Document</h2>
        <p class="text-text-secondary/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The complete Concord of Coexistence framework is available as a research publication.
        </p>
        <a href="/research" class="font-mono text-sm text-terminal-green hover:text-alert-amber transition-colors">
          View in Research section →
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
